176 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (It is my great pleasure to welcome you to the third edition of the UTSRI Undergraduate Case Competition!)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
177 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (In chess, a player can spend years studying openings, anticipating moves, and preparing for every possible scenario. Yet the moment the game begins, one fundamental truth remains - no matter how carefully you plan, you can never control what your opponent does next.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (I believe there is something remarkably similar about scientific research, and perhaps even life itself. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
179 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (Over the next 72 hours, you will be asked to confront complex scientific problems, evaluate competing perspectives, and develop solutions grounded in research and evidence. You will make decisions based on the information available to you, only to discover that new evidence may challenge your original assumptions. What initially appeared straightforward may become considerably more complicated.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
180 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (But that is precisely what makes research so fascinating. The purpose of scientific inquiry is not to prove that our original assumptions were correct. It is to challenge what we believe we know, confront uncertainty, and remain willing to change our minds when the evidence demands it. Sometimes, the greatest intellectual achievement is not discovering that you were right, but having the courage to acknowledge that you were wrong.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
181 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (As we enter another year of this competition, I also want to recognize the extraordinary individuals who have made this event possible. Behind every case, every presentation, and every detail of the conference lies the dedication of our Executive Committee, organizing team, and volunteers. Their hard work continues to transform what began as an ambitious idea into an opportunity for students across Canada to challenge themselves and pursue their academic interests.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
182 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (To our participants, I encourage you to remain curious, trust your teammates, and approach every challenge with an open mind. Remember that while you cannot always control the circumstances you face, you can always decide how you respond to them.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
183 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (And most of the time, those decisions matter far more than the outcome itself.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
184 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (Thank you for being part of this year's competition. I look forward to seeing the ideas, arguments, and solutions you bring to the table, and I hope this experience leaves you with something far more valuable than simply a result.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
