/T (The 2026 Case Competition is designed to challenge students' scientific knowledge, critical thinking, research, and presentation skills. Working in teams, participants are presented with a complex, real-world STEM case and given 72 hours to research the problem, analyze evidence, and develop innovative, evidence-based solutions. Each team must submit a slide deck and an abstract of fewer than 200 words before the competition. )
/E (The 2026 Case Competition is designed to challenge students' scientific knowledge, critical thinking, research, and presentation skills. Working in teams, participants are presented with a complex, real-world STEM case and given 72 hours to research the problem, analyze evidence, and develop innovative, evidence-based solutions. Each team must submit a slide deck and an abstract of fewer than 200 words before the competition. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [8]
