/P 129 0 R
/T (The competition consists of two rounds. In the first round, teams present their solutions to a panel of judges in a 10-minute presentation, followed by a 5-minute Q&A and feedback session. In the second round, known as the Pivot Challenge, teams receive a new challenge related to their original case and have 150 minutes to adapt their proposals before delivering a 5-minute presentation. This format tests not only students' academic abilities, but also their adaptability, decision-making, teamwork, and communication skills under pressure.)
